### Page 4 of 10

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:

The Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and City of Cheyenne Council Members
FROM:

Jason Sanchez, Community Recreation and Events Director
DATE:

September 1, 2022
SUBJECT:
Civic Center Request from General Fund Reserves

Beginning on January 1, 2022, our events division will have managed over 100 large-scale events
within Community Recreation & Events by the end of the year. Almost half of these were hosted
outside of the Civic Center and were either directly managed or facilitated by Civic Center staff.
Some of these events include but are not limited to Fridays on the Plaza, Culture X, Cheyenne
Hispanic Festival, Brewfest, Pancake Breakfast, Arts Fest, and many more. Our team is heavily
relied upon for these events due to their specialized skill sets in event management, marketing and
advertising, technical production, and safety.
In 2019 we had five full-time Civic Center employees facilitating event management, and today
we are down to four. The roles that were lost to the reduction-in-force were critical to the overall
operation and have been absorbed by the remaining four employees. These four employees have
not only excelled in taking over these roles but, in doing so, have significantly improved the quality
and experience of these events. Although this team is continuously reaching new heights, the
demands of these successes require more full-time staff, and in addition, we need to retain the
specialized staff that we have.
After payment of the audio equipment, the Civic Center’s cash balance will be negative.  However,
the need for adding additional employees remains critical. Prior to Covid, we were able to identify
where we were missing the mark in our programming and developed a strategic plan that would
have addressed those areas of opportunity. As we come out of Covid, our team is working to
reinstate that strategy. We are re-evaluating our approach to high-risk investments, pursuing
opportunities that appeal to our target market, identifying ways to make the venue more accessible
for public use, and cutting costs of production by investing in our own equipment. While our team
is moving forward with this plan, it remains imperative to our global operations to add to and retain
our events staff. We strongly believe in the success of our vision, the future of the Civic Center,
and our goals for the community as a Department.
As a department, through diligent fiscal stewardship, we are reverting $418,267 out of the
approved FY22 General Fund operating budget of $7,893,338.  I am respectfully requesting your
support to reappropriate $314,611 of that balance to cover the expense of a Box Office Manager
position and the Civic Center deficit.
```

